[0m[32m[+][39m [36mParameter[39m AccountPoolOuName [90mAccountPoolOuName[39m: [32m{"Type":"String","Default":"","Description":"A custom name to provide for the top-level Innovation Sandbox account pool Organizational Unit (OU) (value if left empty: <namespace>_InnovationSandboxAccountPool). Changing this value on an existing deployment renames the live organizational unit in AWS Organizations (the OU ID is unchanged); update it deliberately."}[39m[0m
[0m[33m[~][39m [36mParameter[39m IsbManagedRegions [90mIsbManagedRegions[39m: [31m{"Type":"CommaDelimitedList","AllowedPattern":"^[a-z]{2}(-[a-z]+-\\d{1})(,[ ]*[a-z]{2}(-[a-z]+-\\d{1}))*$","ConstraintDescription":"Must be a comma-separated list of valid AWS Region codes, e.g., us-east-1,eu-west-1","Description":"Provide list of AWS Regions to limit the use to specific regions."}[39m to [32m{"Type":"CommaDelimitedList","AllowedPattern":"^[a-z]{2}(-[a-z]+-\\d{1})(,[ ]*[a-z]{2}(-[a-z]+-\\d{1}))*$","ConstraintDescription":"Must be a comma-separated list of valid AWS Region codes, e.g., us-east-1,eu-west-1","Description":"Comma-separated list of AWS Regions where sandbox accounts can run workloads. Enable an opt-in Region in the hub account and every sandbox account before you add it here, and in new accounts before you register them. After you change this list, update the Compute stack with a new ForceConfigurationUpdate value."}[39m[0m
[0m[33m[~][39m [36mParameter[39m BedrockInferenceProfilePatterns [90mBedrockInferenceProfilePatterns[39m: [31m{"Type":"CommaDelimitedList","Default":"","AllowedPattern":"^$|^arn:aws:bedrock:[a-z0-9*-]+:[0-9*]+:inference-profile/[a-zA-Z0-9.*:_-]+$","ConstraintDescription":"Must be empty or a comma-separated list of Bedrock inference profile ARN patterns (e.g., arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/*). Each entry must include the inference-profile/ segment. Overly broad patterns like arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:* are not allowed.","Description":"Allow Bedrock cross-region inference by specifying inference profile ARN patterns that are exempt from the region deny SCP. When empty, all cross-region Bedrock calls are blocked by the region restriction SCP. Example patterns: arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/* (all profiles), arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/us.* (US profiles only)."}[39m to [32m{"Type":"CommaDelimitedList","Default":"arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/*","AllowedPattern":"^$|^arn:aws:bedrock:[a-z0-9*-]+:[0-9*]+:inference-profile/[a-zA-Z0-9.*:_-]+$","ConstraintDescription":"Must be empty or a comma-separated list of Bedrock inference profile ARN patterns (e.g., arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/*). Each entry must include the inference-profile/ segment. Overly broad patterns like arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:* are not allowed.","Description":"Comma-separated list of Amazon Bedrock inference profile ARN patterns that the Region restriction SCP exempts, so cross-Region inference can reach Regions outside your managed Regions. The default, arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/*, allows all inference profiles. To allow fewer, list specific patterns, for example arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/us.* for US profiles and arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/global.* for global profiles. If you leave this parameter empty, the SCP blocks all cross-Region Bedrock inference, and Sandbox Spaces can't run models that use cross-Region inference profiles."}[39m[0m

